  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 312 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorm chances increase to 30% on Wednesday night,\n40% on Thursday, and at least 60% on Thursday night as the front pushes\ninto northern Oklahoma and becomes nearly stationary. Medium probabilities\n(to near 40%) extend to the I-40 corridor by Thursday evening. Severe\nstorm potential is being monitored for Thursday, as well, as inverted-V\nsoundings could lead to gusty winds with any storms.\n\nGiven the increasing trend in POPs, it is not surprising that uncertainty\nin high temperatures is also increasing on Thursday through Saturday.\nHigh temperatures have decreased over northern Oklahoma on Thursday,\nand may continue to trend that way if precipitation chances hold or\nincrease. A nearly stationary front setup has an inherent risk of leading\nto excessive rainfall, but the current uncertainties (e.g., frontal\nlocation, timing, and rain chances) are too high at this point to say\nflash flooding will be a concern.\n\nOther than low rain chances this weekend (primarily Saturday), seasonable\ntemperatures are anticipated.\n\nThompson",
